#: src/dependencies.md:1
msgid "Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:3
msgid "Dependencies run before recipes that depend on them:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:19
msgid ""
"In a given invocation of `just`, a recipe with the same arguments will only "
"run once, regardless of how many times it appears in the command-line "
"invocation, or how many times it appears as a dependency:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:43
msgid ""
"Multiple recipes may depend on a recipe that performs some kind of setup, "
"and when those recipes run, that setup will only be performed once:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:64
msgid ""
"Recipes in a given run are only skipped when they receive the same arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:81
msgid "Running Recipes at the End of a Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:83
msgid ""
"Normal dependencies of a recipe always run before a recipe starts. That is "
"to say, the dependee always runs before the depender. These dependencies are "
"called “prior dependencies”."
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:87
msgid ""
"A recipe can also have subsequent dependencies, which run immediately after "
"the recipe and are introduced with an `&&`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:104 src/dependencies.md:137
msgid "…running _b_ prints:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:118
msgid "Running Recipes in the Middle of a Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:120
msgid ""
"`just` doesn’t support running recipes in the middle of another recipe, but "
"you can call `just` recursively in the middle of a recipe. Given the "
"following `justfile`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dependencies.md:151
msgid ""
"This has limitations, since recipe `c` is run with an entirely new "
"invocation of `just`: Assignments will be recalculated, dependencies might "
"run twice, and command line arguments will not be propagated to the child "
"`just` process."
msgstr ""
